#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# solve_values

#% text
# `solve_values(eq, x)` gives the values of the solutions of `eq` for `x`, as a list `[a, b, ...]`.

#% text
# `solve_values(eqs, [x, y, ...])` gives one list of values per solution, `[[a1, b1, ...], ...]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It takes the same equations, domains and options as `solve`, and gives the values of `solve`'s rules in the order of the unknowns.

#% item
# An unknown that a solution does not determine is its own value.

#% item
# Conditional values (`conditional_expression(v, c)`) and generated parameters `c(1)`, ... are kept as `solve` gives them.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The two roots of a quadratic with a parameter:

#% cell
solve_values(x^2 + a*x + 1 == 0, x)
#% output
#= [(1/2)*(-a - (-4 + a^2)^(1/2)), (1/2)*(-a + (-4 + a^2)^(1/2))]

#% text
# The solutions of a system, one list per solution:

#% cell
solve_values(x^2 + y^2 == 2 and x - y == 1, [x, y])
#% output
#= [[(1/2)*(1 - 3^(1/2)), (1/2)*(-1 - 3^(1/2))], [(1/2)*(1 + 3^(1/2)), (1/2)*(-1 + 3^(1/2))]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Over the reals and the integers:

#% cell
solve_values((x^4 - 1)*(x^4 - 4) == 0, x, reals)
#% output
#= [-1, 1, -2^(1/2), 2^(1/2)]

#% cell
solve_values(x^2 + 2*y^3 == 3681 and x > 0 and y > 0, [x, y], integers)
#% output
#= [[15, 12], [41, 10], [57, 6]]

#% text
# An underdetermined system: the free unknown is its own value.

#% cell
solve_values(x + y == 1, [x, y])
#% output
#= [[1 - y, y]]

#% text
# A periodic equation: every solution, with a generated integer parameter:

#% cell
solve_values(sin(x) == 1/3, x)
#% output
#= [conditional_expression(pi - asin(1/3) + 2*pi*c(1), element(c(1), integers)), conditional_expression(asin(1/3) + 2*pi*c(1), element(c(1), integers))]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The values are those of `solve`'s rules:

#% cell
solve_values(x^2 == 4, x) == map(s => x /. s, solve(x^2 == 4, x))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `solve`, `n_solve_values`, `roots`
